cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Lewis: International Economics Analysis Platform"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Anderson
    given-names: Nicholas
    email: nickawebbox@gmail.com
    affiliation: "The New School for Social Research"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"  # Nick to fill
repository-code: "https://github.com/andenick/lewis"
abstract: >-
  A research reference implementation for international economics, combining
  Balance of Payments (BPM6-aligned), Flow of Funds, and cross-border
  value-transfer data. Integrates 116,000+ observations spanning 79 years
  (1945-2024) for the United States, United Kingdom, and Germany, with a complete
  R-to-Python replication of two advanced data-science projects. Includes
  multi-country comparative analysis, historical-event studies, a US deep dive,
  and a publication-quality visualization suite.
keywords:
  - international-economics
  - balance-of-payments
  - flow-of-funds
  - bpm6
  - capital-flows
